[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Templating Engines in PHP: Twig and Blade"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Templating engines are essential tools for PHP developers, allowing for a clean separation of presentation logic from application logic. This tutorial explores two popular PHP templating engines: Twig and Blade."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"What are Templating Engines?"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Templating engines provide a syntax to write templates that are then compiled into PHP code. They offer features like template inheritance, automatic escaping, and control structures, making it easier to create and maintain dynamic web pages."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Twig"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Twig is a flexible, fast, and secure template engine for PHP. It's developed by SensioLabs, the creators of the Symfony framework. Twig's syntax is inspired by Jinja2 and Django templates."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Installation"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can install Twig using Composer:"},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"composer require twig/twig"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Usage"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Here's a simple example of using Twig:"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"// Load Twig
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';

$loader = new \Twig\Loader\FilesystemLoader('templates');
$twig = new \Twig\Environment($loader);

// Data to pass to the template
$data = [
    'name' => 'John Doe',
    'age' => 30
];

// Render the template
echo $twig->render('index.html.twig', $data);"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Create a 'templates' directory and an 'index.html.twig' file with the following content:"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Twig Example</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hello, {{ name }}!</h1>
    <p>You are {{ age }} years old.</p>
</body>
</html>"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Features of Twig"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Template Inheritance: Allows you to define a base template and extend it in other templates."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic Escaping: Protects against XSS vulnerabilities by automatically escaping output."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Filters: Modify variables before outputting them (e.g., `{{ name|upper }}`)."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Functions: Call PHP functions from within your templates (e.g., `{{ date('Y-m-d') }}`)."},{"order":20,"type":"subheading","text":"Blade"},{"order":21,"type":"paragraph","text":"Blade is the simple yet powerful templating engine provided with the Laravel framework. Unlike some PHP templating engines, Blade does not restrict you from using plain PHP code in your views. All Blade views are compiled into plain PHP code and are cached until they are modified, meaning Blade adds essentially zero overhead to your application."},{"order":22,"type":"subheading","text":"Installation"},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"Blade is included with Laravel, so no separate installation is required if you are using Laravel."},{"order":24,"type":"subheading","text":"Basic Usage"},{"order":25,"type":"paragraph","text":"Create a Blade view file (e.g., 'resources/views/greeting.blade.php') with the following content:"},{"order":26,"type":"code","text":"<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Blade Example</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hello, {{ $name }}!</h1>
    <p>You are {{ $age }} years old.</p>
</body>
</html>"},{"order":27,"type":"paragraph","text":"In your Laravel route or controller, pass data to the view:"},{"order":28,"type":"code","text":"Route::get('/greeting', function () {
    $data = [
        'name' => 'John Doe',
        'age' => 30
    ];

    return view('greeting', $data);
});"},{"order":29,"type":"subheading","text":"Key Features of Blade"},{"order":30,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Template Inheritance: Define sections in your layout and extend them in child views using `@extends` and `@section` directives."},{"order":31,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Control Structures: Use directives like `@if`, `@else`, `@foreach`, and `@while` for conditional logic and loops."},{"order":32,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Components: Create reusable UI elements using Blade components."},{"order":33,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Escaping: Blade automatically escapes output using double curly braces `{{ $variable }}`. Use `{!! $variable !!}` to output unescaped content (use with caution!)."},{"order":34,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":35,"type":"paragraph","text":"Twig and Blade are powerful templating engines that simplify the process of creating dynamic web pages in PHP. Twig is a standalone engine suitable for various PHP projects, while Blade is tightly integrated with the Laravel framework. Choosing the right engine depends on your project's requirements and framework preferences."}]
